# REST-Client-Datei (Visual Studio / Rider / VS Code "REST Client").
# 1) Login ausführen, 2) Token unten bei @token eintragen.

@host = http://localhost:5111
@token = <paste-token-here>

### Health
GET {{host}}/health

### Registrierung
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "demo", "password": "demo-password-123" }

### Login
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "demo", "password": "demo-password-123" }

### Übungen (Standard + eigene)
GET {{host}}/api/exercises
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Eigene Übung anlegen
POST {{host}}/api/exercises
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Sled Push", "category": "Football", "muscleGroup": "Legs", "trackingType": "DistanceTime" }

### Einheit speichern (idempotent über clientId)
POST {{host}}/api/workouts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "workoutType": "Hybrid",
  "clientId": "3f2c1a8e-1111-4c1e-9d2a-000000000001",
  "date": "2026-10-28T17:30:00Z",
  "durationSeconds": 3600,
  "sets": [
    { "exerciseId": 1, "weight": 80, "reps": 8 },
    { "exerciseId": 12, "distance": 30, "time": 4.2 }
  ]
}

### Historie seitenweise (nextCursor aus der Antwort als &cursor= anhängen)
GET {{host}}/api/workouts?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Delta-Sync: alles (ohne since) bzw. nur Änderungen seit dem syncToken der letzten Antwort
GET {{host}}/api/workouts/changes?since=2026-10-29T12:00:00Z
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Komplette Historie (Kompatibilität)
GET {{host}}/api/workouts/history
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
